    10	/**
    11	 * The first-run setup: a full-window flow over the shell. Welcome, engine and Deepgram
    12	 * key, microphone, try it, done. It mirrors the macOS flow (Sources/UsefulVoiceApp/FirstRun),
    13	 * minus the Accessibility step Windows has no equivalent of; the dictation hotkey shows on
    14	 * Try it and Done instead.
    15	 *
    16	 * Failure modes, and where each is handled:
    17	 *  - Key check: a refused key (401/403), a dead network and any other answer are three
    18	 *    messages. Nothing is saved unless the check passes. Editing the field while a check
    19	 *    runs drops that check's answer.
    20	 *  - Forced run (`--force-first-run`): main saves nothing at all; the flow also shows no
    21	 *    saved key, so the claim card appears as designed.
    22	 *  - Microphone denied, then allowed while the step is open: a one-second retry moves on.
    23	 *  - Leaving the microphone step, closing the flow or hiding the window stops the meter.
    24	 *  - Practice dictation fails: the pipeline's own error text shows and Retry re-runs it.
    25	 *  - Window closed mid-flow: nothing is marked completed, so the flow shows again next time.
    26	 */
